- Will the money last?: the money left over each month (the Dashboard's own figure) is answered right on the card "What this answer rests on": "Answer" asks what happens to it (invested for later, it stays in the bank, or it gets spent / not sure), with the amount filled in and yours to change; invested or in the bank becomes an ordinary row on What you save for retirement (into an account you pick or a new $0 one), the notice says what was saved and what it did to the retirement answer; invested, the Dashboard's left-over drops by the same amount; kept in the bank, it stays counted as money in checking and savings; the question comes back after a year, when the left-over moves a lot, or when a new bill leaves less than the answer counts ("Lower it to $1,120").
